ry  innovative and powerful and i think  digital technology is where we need to  be  but  i think that before we embark any  further on you know the encroachment of  ai into justice processes we need rules  and i think we need international rules  because if we're recognizing judgments  from abroad  are we recognizing judgments that aren't  actually the product ultimately of a  human mind and i think these questions  need answers and that's what i'm going  to be helping to lead in my work with  harvard kennedy school amazing we're  almost out of time like 30 seconds to  the end of the show i just wondered if  you had a thought on the scottish  referendum second in the ref 2 what do  you think well i think it's interesting  that nicolas sturgeon's taking it to  court even before she's passed uh  an act of parliament i suggest she's  probably pessimistic that she's going to  be allowed to have the power to have  this referendum a general election is a  general election it's not a referendum  and any attempt by her to pretend  otherwise i think is bogus  how interesting fascinating thank you so  much for taking the time to indulge us  with so much of your time thank you

